  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 16 files required for the analysis, covering both sides of the dependency chain:\n\n**Spring Boot side (detection/auto-config):**\n- `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java` \u2014 the detection logic itself; its `Factory` checks for `org.apache.logging.log4j.core.impl.Log4jContextFactory` on the classpath\n- `LoggingApplicationListener.java` \u2014 orchestrates which `LoggingSystem` gets selected at startup\n- `LoggingSystem.java` / `LoggingSystemFactory.java` \u2014 the SPI lookup mechanism (`SpringFactoriesLoader`)\n- `spring.factories` \u2014 registers the three candidate `LoggingSystemFactory` implementations (Logback, Log4j2, JUL)\n- `LogbackLoggingSystem.java` \u2014 the competing default system, for contrast\n- `spring-boot-starter-logging/build.gradle` and `spring-boot-starter-log4j2/build.gradle` \u2014 the two starters, showing the actual bridge dependency each pulls in (`log4j-to-slf4j` vs `log4j-slf4j2-impl`)\n\n**Log4j2 side (bridge modules):**\n- `log4j-to-slf4j/pom.xml` and `SLF4JProvider.java` \u2014 the Log4j-API\u2192SLF4J bridge (used when Logback is the backend)\n- `log4j-api/pom.xml`, `spi/Provider.java`, `util/ProviderUtil.java` \u2014 the core Provider SPI that bridge modules implement\n- `log4j-slf4j-impl/pom.xml` (SLF4J 1.7 binding) and `log4j-slf4j2-impl/pom.xml` + `SLF4JServiceProvider.java` (SLF4J 2.0 binding) \u2014 the split that resulted from the bridge-module restructuring (SLF4J\u2192Log4j-API direction, used when Log4j2 is the backend)",
